.\" Manpage for ia_download.
.TH IA_DOWNLOAD 1 "2026-10-28" "ia_download 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ia_download \- resilient, resumable downloads from archive.org items
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ia_download.py
.I IDENTIFIER DESTINATION
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads files into DESTINATION, preserving item-relative paths. Partial
files are kept separately until their size and MD5 match the item's metadata,
then renamed into place atomically. Re-run the identical command to resume.
Public downloads need no credentials; configured IA cookies/keys are used
when available.
.PP
Resumed requests validate Content-Range before appending. A server that ignores
Range causes a safe restart. Unsafe paths, symlinks and case-insensitive name
collisions are refused. Existing files with different contents require
confirmation or --yes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Read metadata and compare local files. Write no files, including logs.
.TP
.B --original
Select only files whose metadata source is original.
.TP
.BI --glob " PATTERN"
Include matching remote paths; repeatable. Matching is case-sensitive and *
also matches slash. With no globs, all files are selected.
.TP
.BI --exclude " PATTERN"
Exclude matching remote paths; repeatable, usable without --glob.
.TP
.BI --retries " N"
Attempts per request (default 12), including the first attempt.
.TP
.BI --retry-wait " SEC"
Initial exponential backoff (default 15).
.TP
.BI --max-retry-wait " SEC"
Backoff ceiling before jitter (default 600). Retry-After can extend the delay.
.TP
.BI --wait-between " SEC"
Pause between files (default 0).
.TP
.BI --connect-timeout " SEC"
Connection timeout (default 30).
.TP
.BI --read-timeout " SEC"
Read inactivity timeout (default 60), independent of total file size.
.TP
.BI --state " PATH"
Override DESTINATION/.ia_download/state/IDENTIFIER.json. The destination lock
still applies, regardless of the state path.
.TP
.BI --log " PATH"
Append redacted logs to PATH. Ignored in dry runs.
.TP
.B --yes, -y
Replace differing local files without prompting.
.SH VERIFICATION
Missing metadata sizes/checksums reduce verification to the available fields
and are reported. Files without MD5 restart partial transfers from zero.
Files without either size or MD5 are reused only if unchanged since a download
recorded in the state. Cached verification is invalidated by local changes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I DESTINATION/.ia_download/
Resume state, exclusive locks and partial files. Deleting the state causes
re-hashing and restarts partial files, but does not affect completed downloads.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 complete or no matching files; 1 transfer/local I/O failure; 2 invalid
arguments, unsafe paths or refused overwrite; 130 interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ia_download.py my-item ./files/ --dry-run
ia_download.py my-item ./files/ --glob '*.zip' --log download.log
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ia_repack (1), ia_upload (1)
